    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "BOS 30, PHI 23",
        "text": "Jaylen Brown, who barely acknowledged Jayson Tatum's pregame greeting, picked up two fouls in the quarter. Tatum had 9 points on 3-of-5 shooting and Tyrese Maxey 8 on 3-of-3 as Boston took a seven-point lead."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 62, PHI 51",
        "text": "Paul George closed the half with a three off a Derrick White pass and had 17 points on 7-of-11 shooting at the break. Tatum had 13 and Maxey 12."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 91, PHI 82",
        "text": "Philadelphia outscored Boston 25–14 to open the half and tied it 76–76 with 3:50 left, with Joel Embiid getting 11 of his 16 points at the line. Brown picked up his fourth foul early in the quarter. Boston closed on a 15–6 run and made seven threes in the period, two each from Tatum and Payton Pritchard."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 123, PHI 101",
        "text": "Pritchard hit back-to-back threes and George added another in a 9–0 opening run that made it 100–82 and forced a Philadelphia timeout. George's three and an and-one pushed it to 105–82 with 8:08 left, and Boston won the quarter 32–19."
      }
    ],
